# Review with the hosting administrator; not a drop-in complete TLS config.
# Requires mod_rewrite, mod_proxy and mod_proxy_http. Keep existing TLS settings.
# The Node app should listen privately on 127.0.0.1:3000 under a supervisor.

# Inside the port 80 vhost serving drkpharma.edu.in and www.drkpharma.edu.in:
# RewriteEngine On
# RewriteRule ^ https://drkpharma.edu.in%{REQUEST_URI} [R=301,L,NE]

# Inside the HTTPS www.drkpharma.edu.in vhost (with a valid www certificate):
# RewriteEngine On
# RewriteRule ^ https://drkpharma.edu.in%{REQUEST_URI} [R=301,L,NE]

# Inside the HTTPS drkpharma.edu.in vhost, after keeping its TLS directives:
# ProxyPreserveHost On
# ProxyPass / http://127.0.0.1:3000/
# ProxyPassReverse / http://127.0.0.1:3000/

# This proxies both pre-rendered pages and /api/enquiry to the Node server.
# Do not add a blanket SPA rewrite to index.html: it would produce soft 404s.
# Query strings are preserved by these redirect rules. Check for conflicts with
# existing redirect rules and run apachectl configtest before reloading Apache.
